The platform aims to support the buying and planning of campaigns, based on sales-tracking data.

SPAR  has partnered with  retail media  marketplace operator Footprints AI for the development of the platform.

&ldquo;At SPAR our ambition is to connect the strength of our global SPAR network with the power of local retail entrepreneurship, creating a scalable platform that delivers value for customers, retailers and brand partners alike.&rdquo;

The platform will be available to its retail network of more than 13,500 stores across 50 markets and will comply with privacy and data protection legislation.

The platform aims to connect independent retailers with consumers, enabling both local and international retail campaigns, while ensuring that each market retains autonomy over data, assets and commercial strategies.

In addition, the  AI -powered technology aims to forecast consumer behaviour and trends based on real-time purchases, shopping activities, app behaviour and advertising data.

Wasmuht said, &ldquo;By combining our vast physical presence, shopper relationships and data capabilities with advanced retail media technology, we are evolving our SPAR network into a connected commercial ecosystem that enables brands to engage consumers more effectively across markets while generating new revenue opportunities for SPAR country organisations.&rdquo;

Dan Marc, CEO of Footprints AI, added, &ldquo;The next phase is global marketplace infrastructure: advertisers get a more consistent way to plan, buy, optimise, and measure retail media across markets, while local retailers keep control of their data, assets, and commercial model. That is the shift we are building with SPAR.&rdquo;

